<statement>
<p>Show that</p>

<p>
<md>dq\wedge dp</md>
</p>

<p>is closed.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that</p>

<p>
<md>dq\wedge dp</md>
</p>

<p>is nondegenerate on <m>\R^2</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Compute</p>

<p>
<md>\omega(u,v)</md>
</p>

<p>for</p>

<p>
<md>u=(1,2),
\qquad
v=(4,-1),</md>
</p>

<p>using</p>

<p>
<md>\omega=dq\wedge dp.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Verify that the standard symplectic matrix</p>

<p>
<md>J=
\begin{pmatrix}
0&amp;1\\
-1&amp;0
\end{pmatrix}</md>
</p>

<p>satisfies</p>

<p>
<md>J^2=-I.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain the meaning of</p>

<p>
<md>A^TJA=J.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>What does a symplectomorphism preserve?</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

