curvature invariant associated solely with <m>\omega</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>H(q,p)=\frac{p^2}{2m}+V(q),</md>
</p>

<p>derive Hamilton's equations.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>H(q,p)=\frac12p^2+\frac12q^2,</md>
</p>

<p>find</p>

<p>
<md>\dot q</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>\dot p.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Compute</p>

<p>
<md>\{q,p\}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Compute</p>

<p>
<md>\{p,q\}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Compute</p>

<p>
<md>\{q^3,p^2\}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that</p>

<p>
<md>\{f,f\}=0.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>\{f,H\}=0,</md>
</p>

<p>what does this imply about <m>f</m> along the Hamiltonian flow when <m>f</m> has no
explicit time dependence?</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>\dim Q=4,</md>
</p>

<p>find</p>

<p>
<md>\dim T^*Q.</md>
</p>
